# Where the browser calls the API.
#
# This laptop's address on the office network, not 127.0.0.1. A staff member
# who opens their reset link from another machine loads the app from here —
# and the app would then call 127.0.0.1:5000, meaning *their* machine, where
# nothing is listening. The address has to be one the visitor's browser can
# reach, which is the same address serving them the page.
#
# `ipconfig` shows it if the Wi-Fi hands out a different one. Change it in
# backend/config/dev.ini (frontend_base_url and cors_origins) to match, and
# restart both dev servers — Vite reads this file only at startup.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.29.148:5000/api
